    "public_api_change": "ADDITIVE",
    "schema_diff_summary": "modeline.rs is a private module of document.rs. Its one test module is mod tests. Add the new test function at the end of that module, before its closing brace. Do not write a second mod tests. Change only trailing_policy. Fold the value with to_ascii_lowercase, then keep the same match arms. Do not add a second arm that returns the same policy. Do not write two if arms that return the same value. Combine them with ||. That is clippy::if_same_then_else. Do not touch kate_bool, modeline_ending, or trim_policy. The existing test modeline_maps_the_documented_values stays green. Do not rewrite its assertions. The test trailing_spaces_accept_upper_case uses modeline_overrides. kate: remove-trailing-spaces ALL maps to TrailingSpaces::All. NONE maps to TrailingSpaces::Never. MOD maps to TrailingSpaces::ModifiedLines. Branch from the current tip of main. base_sha records that tip at planning time. If main has moved, use the new tip. Keep the change under about 60 lines. Stay inside this one behavior. Run the full test module named in the commands, not only the new test."
